    "summary": "Submitted the checker-correspondence review for the final executed check, which closed the restart question with a bounded negative result.\n\nContext from the index: three findings are confirmed_in_scope (configuration durability, GetConfiguration index readout, committed configuration without a supporting entry), the fourth check on restart consistency executed (go test exit 0, tests_passed) with checker outcome=holds awaiting correspondence, audit units are now exhausted, and pending_work was otherwise empty.\n\nMeasured events from that run: the admitted attempt recorded one injected StoreLogs failure with its error and a pre-restart committed two-voter configuration at index 3; after restarting over the same stores the node was Leader with a one-voter latest configuration at index 1, committed at index 1, the log entry at index 1 being a LogConfiguration read without error, and the log last index 4.\n\nProduct contents (draft-relative submission.json): a single review item with aspect checker_correspondence and status no_issue_found on artifact 69dd7cd0947a48d198f2628e1fb98113. The rationale ties the fixed inputs to the proposition — the obligation (a restarted server must report only a log-encoded latest configuration), the public restart path (NewRaft over the same stores with a fresh FSM after a clean shutdown), the parameterization actually observed before the restart, the implication oracle, the scenario identity across prerequisite and result, and the observation path — and states plainly that the outcome is a bounded negative result: the property held because the antecedent (a restarted two-voter latest configuration) was false, which excludes the explanation that the unsupported committed configuration persists across a restart and becomes durable behaviour. It also records what remains open (the FSM state that may have applied entries under the lost configuration, and the peer's view), and that the restarted committed configuration index regressed to 1 while the log reached index 4 under the re-derived single-voter configuration. Optional Chinese presentation fields lead with the measurement.\n\nPreflight `validate` returned valid=true with no diagnostics. Acceptance and the final assessment remain with the controller. This run's record now holds three confirmed in-scope violations plus one bounded negative result, with the remaining frontier limited to liveness-shaped residuals and out-of-snapshot questions."
